## Report
Rubric-guided crash reproduction: added a focused unit test in server-http that uses parse_copy_source to accept an overlong key, then calls PgTopology::object_pg. parse_copy_source percent-decodes bucket/key but performs no length validation (crates/server-http/src/http/request.rs:368-409). PgTopology::object_pg calls hash_parts, which asserts total_len <= PG_HASH_STACK_LIMIT (crates/server-core/src/pg.rs:12-17, 74-77). Running the test with a 1200-byte key panics at pg.rs:14 with "PG hash input exceeded validated bound: 1207 > 1109" (see crash output), demonstrating an overlong copy-source value can trigger a server panic when hashed.

